course: dictionary
lesson: 482
title: Artifice: a clever trick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Artifice is a noun, so it names a thing: a trick, or a clever skill. It has two meanings. The first is a clever trick used to fool people. The second is clever skill, or a way of doing things that is not natural.
explain: Look at the words around it. In the book, the aunt asks to be «gagged and bound and dumped down in a corner», so she can say she was attacked and keep her job. She wants people to believe a story that is not true. The book calls her plan a «not very convincing artifice», so artifice means a trick, and not a very good one.
explain: Phrases help too. «By artifice» means by a trick or a clever plan. «Without artifice» means honest and natural, with no tricks at all. Ask yourself: is someone pretending, or being truly themselves?
fact: Artifice is a noun. One is an artifice, and more than one is artifices.
fact: «Artifice» means a clever trick used to fool people.
fact: «Artifice» can also mean clever skill, or a way of doing things that is not natural.
fact: «By artifice» means by a trick or a clever plan.
fact: «Without artifice» means honest and natural, with no tricks.
exercise: The book calls the aunt's plan «a not very convincing artifice». What is an artifice here? | A loud noise in the night | A kind present for a friend | A song sung by the sea | *A clever trick used to fool people
exercise: What does «by artifice» mean? | A sudden shout from the crowd | Near the sea, on a sunny day | By mistake, with no thought at all | *By a trick or a clever plan
exercise: What does «without artifice» mean? | Very loud and bright | *Honest and natural, with no tricks | Hidden under the bed | Full of tricks and lies
test: «The magician's artifice fooled the whole crowd.» What does artifice mean here? | A kind word to the audience | *A clever trick used to fool people | A long walk home | A bright light on the stage
test: Mia says her drawing was made «without artifice». What does she mean? | She drew it with a ruler and a compass | She used a clever trick to fool her teacher | She copied it from a book | *Her drawing was honest and natural, with no tricks
exam: Which sentence uses artifice to mean a clever skill or a way of doing things that is not natural? | The boy made a snowman and left it in the garden | The dog barked at the postman every morning | *The painter's artifice made the flowers look almost real | The fox's artifice was to pretend to be asleep
